==
== <Rates AL0-3=".."/> success rate percent per Ancient Level (0-3) of the
==   crafted item, read by the native handler for its own formula.
==
== <Result Section="" Index="" Level="" /> the crafted item (Mode="Fixed").
==
== <Requirements><Item .../></Requirements> - materials consumed:
==   Section/Index      Item (matches Item.xml).
==   MinLevel/MaxLevel  Required item level range. -1 = any.
==   Count              How many are required.
==   CountMode          0 = that many item slots, 1 = Level+1 stacks
==                       (jewels), 2 = raw Durability units (potions/etc).
==   MinDurability/MaxDurability  -1 = any.
==   Role="EvolutionItem"  Marks which requirement is the base item being
==                       evolved (Mode="Evolution" only).
==
== Mode="Evolution" only:
==   <EvolutionMap><Item FromSection="" FromIndex="" ToSection="" ToIndex=""
==     ResultLevel="" /></EvolutionMap>  what the EvolutionItem turns into.
==   <InheritOptions Level="" Durability="" Skill="" Luck=""
==     AdditionalOption="" ExcellentOptions="" AncientOptions=""
==     HarmonyOptions="" Option380="" SocketOptions="" />  1 = carry that
==     property over from the base item to the result.
==   <Failure DestroyEvolutionItem="" DestroyMaterials="" ReduceLevel="" />
==     what happens on the small failure chance implied by Rates.
== Modify only if you know what you're doing!
============================================================
